Brian,



Got some questions fired at me for the STA 360 estimate, see responses below.  I'm sure you'll have more, feel free to give me a call.



Also - Working with Siemens on the breaker estimate, they gave a +/-30% estimate at 300k each.  That would be for the breaker, frame, disconnects, PTs, relays, and battery.



Questions from ES Estimating Group as the PM team has requested a revised estimate based on the most recent scope :

Please check the dollar amount below, all from previous estimate E-23-373.

  1.  Battery System - $12,106,850.  - no  this is for the 12 Nomad Voyager Eagle LFP BESS Systems $12 million.

     *   Assuming this is the DC Battery for Control this will be captured in the Breaker estimate
  1.  Transportation/Spare Parts - $585,688. - I will remove from estimate

     *   unknown

  1.  Battery labor - $2,553,828, 16,801 mhrs is this for the entire new SS or just for the batteries?

     *   Not sure what this is - Estimate E-23-373, labor amount 16,801 man-hours for installation.  Are the 16,801 man-hours for the install of the batteries only or for the install of the entire SS.   Does not say in the estimate.  I have the labor man-hours for the SS equipment, but I do not know how much labor man-hours to charge to the install of the batteries.

  1.  PCS Units - $832,022 is this for the batteries or is this the cost for the five outdoor standalone feeder cabinets?

     *   Not sure what this is - may be a carry over for the PCS for the BESS - ok will remove from the estimate.  I do have costs for the five feeder control cabinets.

  1.  Step up transformers - $630,371.

     *   Is this Station Service Transformers or GSUs? - GSUs is this amount correct?  E-23-373 estimate had this amount.

  1.  Site Sound Mitigation - $466,766 - is this done? Do I need to include the estimate?

     *   I would carry this as a risk item if its needed or not - OK

  1.  Rental - Spot Generator - $139,700 - Did not see in scope but is included in est. E-23-373, Include in Est. or not?

     *   I don't this this is needed - we are going to put station service transforms in first so we should be good - I will remove from estimate.

Other questions:

  1.  Is it an overhead cable or bus from the wood riser pole to the Siemens Breaker? Size and length?
     *   Overhead cable -25' per phase should cover us on both sides of the breaker - Thank you!

  1.  The three SSVT pad mount transformers, I added three riser structures with foundations. Also add UG cable, 500LF per SSVT.  Let me know if you agree with this.

     *   Should be down to 1 Station Service Transformer pad mount.  500' is plenty - Ok, scope has two pad mount SSVT at 1500 kVA each and one pad mount SSVT 125kVA.  I will reduce to one.

  1.  On the eight wood riser poles, are the breaker disconnect switches located on these poles?

     *   Breaker Disconnects are on the skid for the breaker - Excellent thank you

  1.  PTs (8 locations each side of the Siemens breaker, 24 total) - are they installed on the wood riser poles? or on their own steel supports?

     *   PTs are on the breaker skid - Thank you



Thanks,



